{"ts":"2026-07-30T17:01:25.178Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"6682b76673432e27b62e2ad8","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-yekkvt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Declared intent token budgets are smaller than the smallest projection their own command can emit, so three of five intents return no result at all on this tracker"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The intent layer now enforces its declared budgets at one egress point, and enforcement works. What was never checked is whether a declared budget is reachable. Measured at HEAD on the live 2,215-item tracker: next:execute declares 1200 tokens and its smallest bounded projection measures 1438, so the result is dropped on every invocation. context:orient declares 2400 and its smallest bounded section set measures 8417, a factor of 3.5, and it is still dropped at an explicit 8000. context:handoff declares 2200 and behaves identically. Two further reachable cases have no override at all: pm list --limit 200 --for triage and pm get <id> --depth deep --for inspect both drop the result, and --token-budget exits 2 unknown_option on list, get and search, so the ceiling cannot be raised. Run the same five intents against a two-item sandbox workspace and every one of them fits: next:execute measures 367 of 1200 and context:orient 583 of 2400. The declared numbers were therefore calibrated against a toy corpus, and the product targets millions of items. Three separate contract failures follow. First, degradation is all-or-nothing: the only tier below the full projection is budget_receipt_only, which carries zero rows, so there is no graded descent from many rows to fewer rows. Second, the receipt is self-contradictory: within_budget reports true while budget_exceeded.omitted_result reports true in the same envelope, because the estimate is measured after the payload was deleted, so the only way the receipt is within budget is that nothing was served. Third, the recovery guidance says to repeat the command without --for, which routes the caller to the unprojected form: pm next --json is 12,879 bytes against a 400-byte omission receipt, so the documented escape from a token ceiling costs 32 times more tokens than the failure it escapes."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["conformance","context-management","token-budget"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-30T17:01:25.178Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-30T17:01:25.178Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every declared intent budget is greater than or equal to the measured minimum bounded projection of its own command on a corpus at least the size of the current tracker, and a gate fails the build when it is not; Budget enforcement offers at least one intermediate tier that still carries rows before omission is permitted, and the receipt names the tier actually applied; A response that omits its result never reports within_budget true, and the receipt distinguishes an infeasible declaration from an exceeded one; Recovery guidance for an infeasible budget never instructs a caller to re-run the unprojected command when that form emits more tokens than the projection it replaces; The published evidence table records declared budget, measured minimum projection and applied degradation per intent on both a two-item corpus and the current tracker, so calibration against a toy corpus is visible in review"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"8f80913d1e5c18e3705ca27ac144ca7ba1ec63edd879846f15570d1838c76e0c","message":""}
