{"ts":"2026-07-30T17:18:10.348Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"6682b76673432e27b62e2ad8","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies/2","value":{"id":"pm-sf31yl","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-07-30T17:18:10.164Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:update:dep","author_source":"detected"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-30T17:18:10.348Z"}],"before_hash":"225d8e188a3507bac8ed159426fbcc0cb7565fa949453bb2bbdb12547d74c033","after_hash":"624fe1c88d40ca2434ebb6edc9383a828ce27116be9d3e498f0d0f339c46143c","message":"Calibrating a reachable ceiling depends on the final envelope cost, so per-page amortisation lands first or the calibration is done twice against two different envelopes"}
{"ts":"2026-07-30T17:21:51.508Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"6682b76673432e27b62e2ad8","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-30T17:21:51.508Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-30T17:21:51.507Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Method that found this, reusable for any declared bound: run the identical invocation against a two-item workspace and against the real tracker, and diff the verdicts rather than the outputs. A bound that is satisfied on the small corpus and violated on the large one is a scalar that should have been a function, and the small corpus is the one the number was authored against. A bound violated on both is an ordinary miscalibration. A bound satisfied on both is genuinely scale-invariant and can be left alone.\n\nSecond technique, for the same class: a floor is invisible from the default. Raising the ceiling in steps until content first appears is the only way to measure the smallest form a command can emit, because at the default the response contains no rows to measure. next execute yielded nothing at 1200 and 2000 and content at 4000, which located the floor between 2000 and 4000 and then exactly at 1438 from the receipt. Doing this in the other direction, lowering a working ceiling until output disappears, gives the same number and is cheaper when the default already works."}]}],"before_hash":"624fe1c88d40ca2434ebb6edc9383a828ce27116be9d3e498f0d0f339c46143c","after_hash":"6edacc5b531f6c95a6fa4cab70e12ed2bdf440a4ad84d7ba12dba4ae3f52d78b"}
{"ts":"2026-07-31T06:14:40.384Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"bbccd5ce4f6ac18346c324e7","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:14:40.384Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-31T06:14:40.384Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Still live at HEAD 2026.7.31, verified 2026-07-31. `pm next --for execute` emits budget_exceeded.omitted_result: true alongside within_budget: true in one envelope, with token_budget 1200 and estimated_tokens 79 — the receipt reports the omitted-result payload as within budget, so the two keys in the same envelope assert opposite things. The recovery instruction \"Repeat the original command without --for\" costs 9,259 bytes against the 320-byte refusal."}]}],"before_hash":"6edacc5b531f6c95a6fa4cab70e12ed2bdf440a4ad84d7ba12dba4ae3f52d78b","after_hash":"493357eadd8626f28d8b902626550c931b2e149f9c3a69fd9e9cf140f8953f6c"}
